Feature: Launching
  Pick what to start on the LAUNCH screen, then click LAUNCH. GROUND STATION starts the sim,
  ArduPilot SITL and the console together. SIMULATOR ONLY starts the sim alone. WITH ARDUPILOT
  flies the T1-S VTOL. WITHOUT ARDUPILOT flies the plain T1-S Ranger in the sim. In the
  station, WITHOUT ARDUPILOT gives the sticks to the sim's own modes, and ArduPilot only
  reports. The launcher opens on the station with ArduPilot, in the Alpine Valley.

  [[Running and stopping a program]] tells you what LAUNCH does next.

  Expectation: LAUNCH starts the station with ArduPilot
    Given the launch target is GROUND STATION
    And the flight controller choice is WITH ARDUPILOT
    When the pilot launches
    Then the program in the log is the ground station
    And the sticks of the started station are through ArduPilot

  Expectation: Without ArduPilot, the station gives the sticks to the sim
    The sim flies the plane through its own modes. ArduPilot still runs, for the telemetry,
    but the sim does not use its outputs.

    Given the launch target is GROUND STATION
    And the flight controller choice is WITHOUT ARDUPILOT
    When the pilot launches
    Then the program in the log is the ground station
    And the sticks of the started station are direct

  Expectation: The sim alone with ArduPilot flies the T1-S VTOL
    The sim starts its own ArduPilot: the native build, or the Docker image.

    Given the launch target is SIMULATOR ONLY
    And the flight controller choice is WITH ARDUPILOT
    When the pilot launches
    Then the program in the log is the simulator
    And the plane of the started sim is the T1-S VTOL

  Expectation: The sim alone without ArduPilot flies the T1-S Ranger
    Given the launch target is SIMULATOR ONLY
    And the flight controller choice is WITHOUT ARDUPILOT
    When the pilot launches
    Then the program in the log is the simulator
    And the plane of the started sim is the T1-S Ranger

  Expectation: The place goes to the program
    Given the place choice is CYPRESS
    When the pilot launches
    Then the place of the started program is Cypress

  Expectation: RAY TRACING goes to the program
    Given the ray tracing choice is on
    When the pilot launches
    Then the ray tracing of the started program is on
